      "curator_note": "Generic carbonyl scheme (R, R', CR2): no m/z or intensity printed. The text says electron-pair attraction to the charge site yields the canonical resonance structure R2C+-O• and that 'inductive cleavage of this then gives the alkyl ion and acyl radical'; this canonical form is used here as the precursor. Book draws 1 arc on this canonical form: a single fishhook at the C-R bond. Encoded moves <1> and <2> both originate at that C-R bond (the drawn fishhook), and move <3> (O odd electron into the new C=O pi bond) is an implicit hook required for electron balance, not drawn on this form. (A separate full 2-electron arrow is drawn on the molecular-ion resonance form R2C=O+• shown to its left.) Instantiated as acetone (R=R'=CH3): products CH3+ + CH3-C•=O are the exact complements of the acetone alpha-cleavage of Eq 4.14 (CH3• + CH3CO+), as the text notes. m/z 15.0235 for CH3+ is curator-computed from this instantiation, not printed in the book."
